# Architecture: Infrastructure Layer

- The infrastructure layer must contain technical implementations only.
- Module infrastructure code must live under `app/modules/<module>/infrastructure`.
- SQLAlchemy models must live in `sqlalchemy_models.py`.
- SQLAlchemy repository implementations must live in `sqlalchemy_repositories.py`.
- Infrastructure code must implement contracts defined by the domain or application boundary.
- Infrastructure code may use SQLAlchemy, Redis, JWT libraries, SMTP providers, external APIs, storage providers, and other technical SDKs.
- ORM models must end with `Model`.
- Concrete repository implementations must include their implementation type in the name, such as `SqlAlchemyUserRepository`.
- Do not put business workflows, permission rules, full scenario coordination, or use-case operation ordering in infrastructure code.
- Do not make infrastructure implementations the source of domain contracts. Define the contract inward, then implement it outward.
- Do not expose infrastructure models or SDK DTOs directly to the API or domain layers.
